Fix 1: .dockerignore
Keep .env.example in the build context:

.git
.gitignore
.github
README.md
node_modules
vendor
laravel-app/vendor
laravel-app/node_modules
laravel-app/.env
laravel-app/.env.*
!laravel-app/.env.example
laravel-app/storage/logs/*
laravel-app/storage/framework/cache/*
laravel-app/storage/framework/sessions/*
laravel-app/storage/framework/views/*
The ! line has to come after the .env.* line. Also check that laravel-app/.env.example is committed to git.

Fix 2: Dockerfile (recommended)
This version doesn't need .env.example at all. It also keeps secrets and config caching out of the image.

dockerfile
FROM php:8.2-apache
WORKDIR /var/www/html
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    git unzip libpng-dev libonig-dev libxml2-dev zip curl ca-certificates gnupg \
    && curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | bash - \
    && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends nodejs \
    && docker-php-ext-install pdo_mysql mbstring exif pcntl bcmath gd \
    && curl -sS https://getcomposer.org/installer | php -- --install-dir=/usr/local/bin --filename=composer \
    && a2enmod rewrite headers \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
RUN sed -ri -e 's!/var/www/html!/var/www/html/public!g' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf \
    && sed -ri -e 's!/var/www/html!/var/www/html/public!g' /etc/apache2/apache2.conf
COPY laravel-app/composer.* ./
RUN composer install --no-interaction --no-ansi --no-progress --prefer-dist --optimize-autoloader --no-dev --no-scripts
COPY laravel-app/ ./
RUN composer dump-autoload --no-dev --optimize \
    && npm install --no-fund --no-audit \
    && npm run build \
    && rm -rf node_modules \
    && mkdir -p storage/framework/cache storage/framework/sessions storage/framework/views storage/logs bootstrap/cache \
    && chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html \
    && chmod -R 775 storage bootstrap/cache
COPY docker-entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh
RUN chmod +x /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh
EXPOSE 80
ENTRYPOINT ["docker-entrypoint.sh"]
CMD ["apache2-foreground"]
Create docker-entrypoint.sh at the repo root, next to the Dockerfile, and save it with LF line endings, not CRLF:

sh
#!/bin/sh
set -e
php artisan config:cache
php artisan route:cache
php artisan view:cache
exec "$@"
The storage/framework/* folders are created in the Dockerfile because the .dockerignore excludes their contents. Laravel fails at runtime if they're missing.

Fix 3: HostForge environment variables
Set these in HostForge:

APP_KEY: generate it locally with php artisan key:generate --show. It looks like base64:....
APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
APP_URL
DB_CONNECTION, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_DATABASE, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD
Things that may still break
Vite build needs dev dependencies. npm install installs them, so this is fine. If the build needs PHP packages such as Ziggy, they must not be dev-only.
Migrations. Run php artisan migrate --force from the HostForge console. You can also add it to the entrypoint, but only if there is a single instance.
Node 20. Make sure their package.json engines field doesn't require a different version.
Folder check. If laravel-app/ is a stale duplicate of the root app, they should either point COPY at the right folder or use COPY . ./.